% lps-converted-from: mars_explorer.lps
% This document was written from the LPS program mars_explorer.lps, which says the same thing in the older syntax. The two run alike, and tools/lps_to_le_test.pl checks that they do. The first line above is what keeps the older file from being read as this document's companion, which would run every rule twice.

the target language is: lps.

the maximum time is 12.

the events are:
    *a thing* arrives.
    *a thing* spots rock.
    sunrise.
    sunset.

the actions are:
    *a thing* drives to; known as drive_to.
    *a thing* takes sample; known as take_sample.
    recharge.
    *a thing* transmits; known as transmit.

the fluents are:
    the at is *a thing*; known as at.
    *a thing* is sample taken; known as sample_taken.
    *a thing* is knows rock; known as knows_rock.
    the battery is *a thing*; known as battery.

the knowledge base mars_explorer includes:

initially the at is base
    and the battery is 100.

when a thing arrives
then the at that is a second thing becomes the thing.

when a thing drives to
then the at that is a second thing becomes the thing.

when a thing spots rock
then the thing is knows rock.

when a thing takes sample
then the thing is sample taken.

when recharge
then the battery that is a thing becomes 100.

when a thing drives to
then the battery that is a second thing becomes second thing - 10.

if a thing is knows rock at a time
    and it is not the case that the thing is sample taken at the time
    and the battery is a second thing at the time
    and the second thing > 30
then the thing drives to from the time to a second time
    and the thing takes sample from the second time to a third time
    and the thing transmits from the third time.

it must not be true that
    a thing drives to from a time to a second time
    and a second thing drives to from the time to the second time
    and the thing is different from the second thing.

if the battery is a thing at a time
    and the thing <= 30
then base drives to from the time to a second time
    and recharge from the second time.

it must not be true that
    a thing drives to
    and the battery is a second thing
    and the second thing < 15.


scenario one is:
    ridge spots rock from 2 to 3.
    crater spots rock from 5 to 6.
